; Leg AH -- edit 17, cautious x block 1.  THE FLOOR, and a null result is
; the one this leg is trying to produce.
;
; Edit 17 does not touch chk1().  It adds crctab16[] and rewrites chk3()'s
; body inside #ifdef VICTOR9K; nothing on the block-1 path changed, and the
; only shared cost is 512 bytes of DGROUP that a block-1 transfer never
; reads.  So this leg must REPRODUCE SS16ae leg BX:
;
;     26.50 s elapsed, rxpeak 2,611, rxfull 0, 37,523 wire bytes, 1,236 cps
;
; If it does, two things follow, and they are the reason to spend a leg on
; a result that is supposed to be nothing:
;
;   1. AG's improvement is attributable to chk3() and not to a rebuild.
;      Any binary differs from any other in layout, and SS16w already
;      showed this machine is sensitive to code SIZE in a way most are not
;      (-ot grew far code 9.2% and cost 13% of rxpeak).  A block-1 leg that
;      moved would mean the rebuild itself changed something, and AG's
;      delta would then be unattributable.
;   2. It gives AG a target.  The whole argument for edit 17 is that it
;      buys most of block 1's speed while KEEPING CRC-16.  How much of it
;      is exactly AG-versus-AH, measured today, on one binary.
;
; Read, in this order:
;
;   1. cmp RCVAH.DAT rcvah.dat -- byte-exact.
;   2. rxfull -- must be 0.  BX was 0 and block 1 has never overflowed.
;   3. rxpeak against BX's 2,611.  The three block-1 legs in SS16ae spread
;      only 38 counts (2,630 / 2,592 / 2,611), so this is a tight
;      instrument and a large move here is a real signal.
;   4. elapsed= against BX's 2,650 cs.
;
; Prediction: everything within SS16ae's block-1 spread.  A NULL RESULT IS
; THE PASS.  If this leg comes back faster than BX, do not celebrate --
; investigate, because edit 17 has no mechanism to speed up block 1 and an
; unexplained gain means the comparison is measuring something else.

set line /dev/tty.usbserial-ABBFKXM1
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 1
log packets s16afAH.pkt
send rcvah.dat
statistics
